cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the AidPage typology (도감) or its data, please cite it as below. 이 유형화·데이터를 쓰시면 아래와 같이 인용해 주세요."
type: dataset
title: "AidPage Atlas — rule-based, rank-free multi-lens profiles of Korean municipalities (v1.4) with national aid thresholds and recorded outcomes"
version: "dex-v1.4"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
authors:
  - given-names: Jihwan
    family-names: Oh
    alias: 5-Jihwan
repository-code: "https://github.com/5-Jihwan/aidpage"
url: "https://5-jihwan.github.io/aidpage/atlas.html"
abstract: >-
  Rule-based typology of 255 Korean municipal units (si/gun/gu) across natural hazards
  (flood history, landslide/slope, coastal contact, drought zones), a social hazard
  (traffic), unordered vulnerability traits, and institutional (ordinance) holdings.
  Thresholds are national top-quartile cut-offs within the same unit class; no composite
  score or ranking is produced. v1.4 adds the national recovery-aid threshold layer
  (fiscal-capacity bands under Regulation art. 5①, in force from 2024-11-19) and recorded
  outcomes from the Disaster Yearbook 2012–2024 (central subsidy events, special disaster
  area declarations, severe-damage events). Sensitivity specifications (p70/p80 thresholds,
  229-unit aggregation) are shipped alongside for review.
keywords:
  - disaster risk
  - Korea
  - municipal typology
  - administrative burden
  - fiscal capacity
  - regression discontinuity
